Subject: Cantor Nested Outer Host Identity P0 Solution

@ [solution_uuid] d56f76dc-b7c7-4c06-ad80-709c311db978
@ [canonical_uuid] 762ca2d3-c279-4e73-ad1c-990f31950a28

& [Implementation]
  + one pure cantor_core module defines strict request process model bounds envelope lifecycle authority denial fault and deterministic machine forms
  + four session host process and model identities must remain distinct
  + process state is only declared_unobserved and model state is only declared_unloaded
  + request and envelope SHA256 identities are domain-separated and all envelope correspondence is rederived

& [Security]
  + exact unresolved truths and six fixed capability denials prevent identity from becoming physical or execution authority
  + unknown fields malformed digests invalid text widened bounds missing evidence collisions altered states output mutation denial removal and request substitution fail closed
  + compilation is atomic and performs no filesystem environment clock process network provider model persistence or external effect action

& [ProductPosition]
  + NHC-01 is the first reusable nested-host identity seam, not a running agent
  + the current user target is separately sequenced as SOP boot to bounded work to verified update to succeeding SOP proposal
  + self-authorship remains attributable proposal formation and never self-signature or self-activation
